The 3D Gaussian Splatting trainer is an independent Swift and Metal
implementation of published methods. It contains no source code from the
original 3D Gaussian Splatting (Inria/MPII) or Mip-Splatting implementations,
which are licensed for non-commercial use only, nor from LichtFeld Studio
(GPL-3.0). It follows these publications and projects:

- 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering (Kerbl et al., 2023)
- Mip-Splatting: Alias-free 3D Gaussian Splatting (Yu et al., 2024)
- LichtFeld Studio's MRNF densification defaults (https://github.com/MrNeRF/LichtFeld-Studio)
- PPISP, Physically-Plausible ISP (https://github.com/nv-tlabs/ppisp, Apache-2.0)
- Gaussian Splatting on the Move (Seiskari et al., 2024) for the experimental
  capture-motion model
- Speedy-Splat (Hanson et al., 2025) for the idea of listing a splat only in the
  tiles it actually intersects
- Taming 3DGS (Mallick et al., 2024) for the sparse Adam tested as an experiment

